repository-code: https://github.com/gitdeeper15/aethermesh
abstract: >
  AetherMesh v2.0.0 is the reference implementation of the AetherMesh
  architecture specified in v1.0.0: a fully decentralized peer-to-peer
  synchronization framework for autonomous agent networks that modify
  shared codebases and metadata DAGs. It implements a tripartite
  architecture: (1) specialized conflict-free replicated data types
  (CRDTs) for code structures and semantic metadata; (2) epidemic
  gossip protocols for low-latency, resilient propagation; and (3) a
  lightweight Byzantine fault tolerance (BFT) admission layer that
  verifies remote deltas before they enter the local join-semilattice.
  The reference implementation includes 15 Python modules, 107 tests
  (79% coverage), and 3 reproducible experiments. The v1.0.0 paper
  remains the authoritative record; v2.0.0 adds a reference
  implementation alongside it. No real-world deployment has been
  evaluated.
